                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "c80e15ab-1865-4583-bd16-8ee43ec0d39e",
                        "entry_id": "d0b7d8a8-d79f-385b-92a2-1751a6dc9c04",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "раду́шиях"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "73243ecb-328f-39aa-9412-deba347910c3",
                        "entry_id": "d0b7d8a8-d79f-385b-92a2-1751a6dc9c04",
                        "glosses": [
                            "сердечное, ласковое отношение, соединенное с гостеприимством, с готовностью помочь, оказать услугу"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e8a8d2e-9f9b-4f0e-85a2-e52978aca306",
                                "sense_id": "73243ecb-328f-39aa-9412-deba347910c3",
                                "text": "Проявить радушие."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a7d8535c-e55c-4a88-a3cd-5793aa364d3f",
                                "sense_id": "73243ecb-328f-39aa-9412-deba347910c3",
                                "text": "Отнестись с необыкновенным радушием."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1994ecb3-4dea-4905-8a4f-9332feca758c",
                                "sense_id": "73243ecb-328f-39aa-9412-deba347910c3",
                                "text": "Всё-таки, видно, не все было в порядке с его радушием, потому что на лице красивой Лиды вдруг появилось выражение растерянности и она почему-то оглянулась на пустую, залитую солнцем лестничную площадку, словно вдруг усомнилась, туда ли она попала."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e9c903ed-85bb-4f93-8d5d-36089f722846",
                        "source_entry_id": "d0b7d8a8-d79f-385b-92a2-1751a6dc9c04",
                        "source_sense_id": "73243ecb-328f-39aa-9412-deba347910c3",
                        "target_lang_word": "hospitality",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hospitality",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b3fcf50c-247e-363c-8692-6a35b3186e82",
                                        "entry_id": "1842c77f-5d73-3142-acdc-d02f5fbe6eef",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act or service of welcoming, receiving, hosting, or entertaining guests; an appropriate attitude of openness, respect, and generosity toward guests."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "199fb305-dccb-4a5a-abd2-988bd8fd5a1e",
                                                "sense_id": "b3fcf50c-247e-363c-8692-6a35b3186e82",
                                                "text": "Please thank our hosts for their hospitality during the week that we stayed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "60075b7c-1227-4f68-b1fa-491e92318fea",
                                                "sense_id": "b3fcf50c-247e-363c-8692-6a35b3186e82",
                                                "text": "\"Quarrels!\" said Charles; \"do not use so disagreeable a word. I am thinking of nothing but the thanks I owe Lord Avonleigh for his hospitality\"—Lord Avonleigh bent to the very edge of the table—\"and the favours I am about to ask.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02d94b7c-4fae-457d-90d5-8e622c6acfa3",
                                                "sense_id": "b3fcf50c-247e-363c-8692-6a35b3186e82",
                                                "text": "In Ancient Times, as Story tells, / The Saints would often leave their Cells, / And ſtrole about, but hide their Quality, / To try good Peoples Hoſpitality."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48ae4569-51bb-4d8e-a22d-bb9beb762db3",
                                                "sense_id": "b3fcf50c-247e-363c-8692-6a35b3186e82",
                                                "text": "Mr Venus, reminded of the duties of hospitality, produced some rum."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91c88941-3df6-4ac8-85f8-8e134cffdd46",
                                                "sense_id": "b3fcf50c-247e-363c-8692-6a35b3186e82",
                                                "text": "We were over the border here, into Northern Ireland, and the post office had a very English atmosphere. It was pleasant, too, much as we enjoyed the hospitality of the Republic, to be buying stamps with the Queen's head on them, and to be posting our cards in a red pillar-box, instead of a green one."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "43bc7237-395f-3d82-a39a-1dd6627df7bf",
                                        "entry_id": "1842c77f-5d73-3142-acdc-d02f5fbe6eef",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The business of providing catering, lodging and entertainment service; the industry which includes the operation of hotels, restaurants, and similar enterprises."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "371af1a1-fab0-4f66-9d1f-7b221636cbaa",
                                                "sense_id": "43bc7237-395f-3d82-a39a-1dd6627df7bf",
                                                "text": "After graduating from college, she found a job in hospitality."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "36342425-22c3-37f5-8837-ef17c6e80314",
                                        "entry_id": "1842c77f-5d73-3142-acdc-d02f5fbe6eef",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The food, drink, and entertainment given to customers by a company or organization or provided to visitors by a private host."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "81ba785e-6af9-43a5-86f3-c11d08cf15c5",
                        "source_entry_id": "d0b7d8a8-d79f-385b-92a2-1751a6dc9c04",
                        "source_sense_id": "73243ecb-328f-39aa-9412-deba347910c3",
                        "target_lang_word": "cordiality",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cordiality",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a0ebf90b-dccc-365e-bdee-a90526076f00",
                                        "entry_id": "9aaf0e43-fe1a-3961-8ba3-b6ddd4913d78",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality of being cordial."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "79493a29-74d4-469e-acdb-8a8073ac362f",
                                                "sense_id": "a0ebf90b-dccc-365e-bdee-a90526076f00",
                                                "text": "Upon my entrance, Usher rose from a sofa on which he had been lying at full length, and greeted me with a vivacious warmth which had much in it, I at first thought, of an overdone cordiality—of the constrained effort of the ennuyé man of the world."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a651b67-3932-42ea-be93-f26e123d80c3",
                                                "sense_id": "a0ebf90b-dccc-365e-bdee-a90526076f00",
                                                "text": "Adam gave her—the spaniel, not Mrs. Florin—a gentle prod with his foot and a lump of sugar. She licked his shoe with evident cordiality. Adam was not above feeling flattered by friendliness in dogs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "049a715e-8e5c-35dc-9fa1-68265961868e",
                                        "entry_id": "9aaf0e43-fe1a-3961-8ba3-b6ddd4913d78",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A friendly utterance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e1901ae-c290-46ec-9dd5-f93971405549",
                                                "sense_id": "049a715e-8e5c-35dc-9fa1-68265961868e",
                                                "text": "to exchange cordialities with people"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2851b62d-5e0d-49fd-947a-7e39c93af334",
                                                "sense_id": "049a715e-8e5c-35dc-9fa1-68265961868e",
                                                "text": "Lucia rivalled these cordialities with equal fervour and about as much sincerity."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a4af2b9c-94fb-46c8-90d2-8d67265545d0",
                        "source_entry_id": "d0b7d8a8-d79f-385b-92a2-1751a6dc9c04",
                        "source_sense_id": "73243ecb-328f-39aa-9412-deba347910c3",
                        "target_lang_word": "geniality",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "geniality",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c0e57bf9-af7b-310a-8f82-6e6902d8e21d",
                                        "entry_id": "2f45e0c2-0162-38e3-bf01-f7692b985b9b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality of being genial; friendly cheerfulness; warmth of disposition and manners."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e52bd1f5-96a3-4a30-993f-0241564f1b73",
                                                "sense_id": "c0e57bf9-af7b-310a-8f82-6e6902d8e21d",
                                                "text": "Sometimes this throat uttered Yes, sometimes it uttered No; sometimes it made inquiries about a time worn denizen of the place. Once it surprised her notions by remarking upon the friendliness and geniality written in the faces of the hills around."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f4060ec-ce30-4126-8470-4c8d25495395",
                                                "sense_id": "c0e57bf9-af7b-310a-8f82-6e6902d8e21d",
                                                "text": "[…] and yet there was such a wilful geniality about him, such a strenuous air of being off duty and forgetting his rank, that no one was ever quite at ease in his presence."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
